process.rule:
1. Read github-branch from task.xml. Verify current branch matches. If not, error and exit. 2. Commit and push: git add .festinalente/tasks/{id}/plan.xml .festinalente/tasks/{id}/task.xml git commit -m "docs({issueNumber}): plan" git push 3. Comment on GitHub Issue with full plan: mcp__GitHub__add_issue_comment — body: "## Planned

```xml
{plan.xml contents}
```" 4. Create Draft PR: mcp__GitHub__create_pull_request — title: "{title}", head: {github-branch}, base: main, draft: true, body: "Closes #{github-issue}

_Draft — not yet implemented._" 5. Add github-pr="#{N}" to task.xml, commit and push: git commit -m "docs({issueNumber}): draft pr" && git push

Update the PR title and body via mcp__GitHub__update_issue (PRs are issues in GitHub's API): 1. Set title to: "{type}({issueNumber}): {short description of changes}" (same commit type and description used in GH-FIN-COMMIT step 4). 2. Set body to: "Closes #{github-issue}

## Summary

{bullet list of changes}

## Test plan

{checklist from acceptance criteria}" 3. Use mcp__GitHub__update_issue with issue_number={PR number from github-pr}.
